# Community files

Read these before you file an issue, open a PR, or treat a GitHub issue. Do not invent a parallel process.

| Task | Source of truth |
| --- | --- |
| Setup, tests, style, commits, PRs | [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md) |
| Conduct | [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md) |
| Security reports | [SECURITY.md](SECURITY.md) |
| Bug reports | `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.md` |
| Pull request body | `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` |
| Treating a GitHub issue | `.cursor/skills/github-issue/SKILL.md` |

- Do not open a public issue for a vulnerability or a conduct report.
- When creating a bug issue, use the bug report template fields and `--label bug`.
- When creating a PR, fill the PR template. Follow `.cursor/rules/pull-requests.mdc`.
- When the user passes a GitHub issue URL or `/github-issue`, follow the github-issue skill.
